    "ai_comment_en": "The region at coordinates 35.61°N, 82.19°E has been evaluated with a total score of 68.3 for the Shackleton Crater rim target. The geology (98.1) and topography (90.7) dimension scores are high; alignment with the target has been achieved, particularly in the parameters of frozen ground with near-surface ice (0.57 on Earth, 0.56 at the target) and average slope (12.55° on Earth, 13.94° at the target). In addition, the aridity level shows similarity (0.93 on Earth, 1.0 at the target).\n\nIn contrast, due to the climate dimension score remaining at 32.9, there are some distinct mismatches and breaking points. The average surface temperature was measured as -5.91 °C on Earth while being -181.3 °C at the target, and this parameter was not found to be similar. Furthermore, gravity is at the level of ~1/6th of Earth's (1.62 m/s²), causing dust and wheel behavior to differ; since the atmosphere is virtually non-existent, there is no wind erosion or heat transfer, and there is no liquid water on the surface with ice existing only in permanent shadows. The region is closed to road access and is remote."
